  "body": "`delegatesFocus` doesn't work well with `autofocus` because  the step 9 of [flush autofocus candidates](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#flush-autofocus-candidates) drops an element if the element is not a focusable area and the delegation happens in the first step of [focusing steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#focusing-steps).\r\n\r\nPossible solutions:\r\n - Factor out the first step of [focusing steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#focusing-steps), and use it from [flush autofocus candidates](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#flush-autofocus-candidates) too, or\r\n - Add a return value to [focusing steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#focusing-steps) indicating success/failure of the focus change. [Flush autofocus candidates](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#flush-autofocus-candidates) calls focusing steps without focusable area check, and checks the return value.\r\n\r\nCc: @rakina @domenic \r\n",
